1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,767
In 2012, NASA's fire record

2
00:00:01,767 --> 00:00:02,760
jumps tenfold.

3
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:03,699
The fires didn't change.

4
00:00:03,699 --> 00:00:04,960
The satellite did.

5
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,323
So we built a machine

6
00:00:06,323 --> 00:00:08,334
that learns how both satellites see,

7
00:00:08,334 --> 00:00:09,360
area by area.

8
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:11,372
Tested on years it never saw,

9
00:00:11,372 --> 00:00:13,536
its error falls from 77% to 14%,

10
00:00:13,536 --> 00:00:15,960
and every value shows its margin.

11
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:16,854
Draw any area:

12
00:00:16,854 --> 00:00:18,792
Zij fits it live in your browser,

13
00:00:18,792 --> 00:00:20,246
and tells emergency teams

14
00:00:20,246 --> 00:00:21,960
if this season is normal.

15
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:24,334
And it reveals what the split record hid:

16
00:00:24,334 --> 00:00:26,261
in the Delta, detected burning rose

17
00:00:26,261 --> 00:00:27,343
after the 2004 ban,

18
00:00:27,343 --> 00:00:29,177
and has halved since 2018.
